# Headers for the STATIC ASSET responses (2026-07-27 ASVS L2 scan, M5).
#
# These never reach `workers/app.ts`: Cloudflare's ASSETS binding answers a
# matching path before the Worker runs, so every header the Worker adds — CSP
# included — is absent from `/assets/*`. Measured in production: those responses
# carried none of the six.
#
# `_headers` is the supported way to attach headers to asset responses. Vite
# copies this file from `public/` into `build/client/`, which is the directory
# `wrangler.jsonc` declares as `assets.directory`.
#
# Scoped to `/assets/*` deliberately, rather than `/*`: everything else on this
# host is answered by the Worker, which sets its own headers, and a blanket rule
# here would be a second place those values live.

/assets/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
